WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.209 --> 00:00:04.859
Chrollo Lucilfer embodies both Jesus and the
devil.

00:00:04.859 --> 00:00:10.211
And yet at the bottom of his, at first glance
paradoxical view on life and people, there

00:00:10.211 --> 00:00:17.220
is an incredibly strong and surprisingly un-religious
message about power and how it tends to warp

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:31.349
good intentions and love into cruelty and
inhumanity. This makes Chrollo a case study

00:00:31.349 --> 00:00:36.650
of extremist human behavior and given all
the deep concepts explored in his character,

00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:43.030
it is no wonder that its easy to misunderstand
what his character is actually about.

00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:49.030
Is he a a higher being with a higher purpose,
as his power and determination suggests, or

00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:55.240
simply a fanatic that uses his beliefs as
justification for his horrendous deeds? Because

00:00:55.240 --> 00:01:00.980
to me, belonging to the trinity of godly villains
that Togashi has created, each of them explores

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:04.320
a different aspect of power and evil.

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:14.090
As you'll remember from his video, Hisoka
is an exploration of hedonism and sociopathy.

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:24.090
Meruem deconstructs the idea that humanity
is special as well as the dark implications

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:39.750
of pride and arrogance. And effortlessly continuing
that pattern, I think that Chrollo explores

00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:45.760
the themes of power and evil from a very unique
perspective as well: Religion. Or to be more

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:49.170
precise, the believe into a higher purpose.

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:54.409
To me, Chrollo highlights both the best and
the worst in religious practice and believe.

00:01:54.409 --> 00:02:00.340
In a story exploring human morality, with
Chrollo Togashi makes the most direct statement

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:05.590
as to what it means to be morally good and
bad. And no matter whether you are Cristian

00:02:05.590 --> 00:02:12.530
or not, or actually religious or not, understanding
Chrollo will show you why you love Hunter

00:02:12.530 --> 00:02:17.820
x Hunter so much. Because as you'll find out,
I'm a bit of a fan myself.

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:23.140
Now, One thing I noticed quickly after getting
more and more into anime, was that religious

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:29.330
themes are not exactly a rarity in the genre
and given Japan's own culture, it's no big

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:34.940
surprise that especially Zen Buddhism and
Shintoism are part of many popular stories.

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:40.260
Hunter x Hunter is no exception to this rule,
only that as usual, I believe it deals with

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:46.000
the associated ideas and concepts on a much
more fundamental and at least for me, much

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:48.200
more interesting level.

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:54.150
However with Chrollo, it also explores a religion
that I rarely see integrated into other stories,

00:02:54.150 --> 00:03:07.140
at least at such a level of understanding.
Christianity. You definitely already know

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:12.030
all the obvious connections that associate
it with Chrollo. There is the reverse cross

00:03:12.030 --> 00:03:16.690
tattooed in perfect post Malone fashion on
his forehead, that is also stitched on the

00:03:16.690 --> 00:03:23.470
back of his robe. It's associated both with
saint Peter, but also with the anti-christ,

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:28.700
also known as the devil or Lucifer, which
who would have thought, is just one letter

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:30.750
short of Chrollo's last name.

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:35.660
The phantom troupe, that as we will see is
a big part of Chrollo's identity, consists

00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:51.090
of 13 members, just as Jesus and his 12 apostles,
with Hisoka representing Judas and his betrayal.

00:03:51.090 --> 00:03:56.290
[...] And just like Jesus, Chrollo sees himself
on a divine mission, even though he doesn't

00:03:56.290 --> 00:04:01.790
seem to know what that mission is. And even
if he knew at some point, he seems to have

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:08.790
forgotten it by now. Being willing to sacrifice
himself for his followers and taking no real

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:14.660
interest in worldly possessions, he didn't
follow my expectations of a typical bad guy,

00:04:14.660 --> 00:04:27.639
but at the same time clearly does horrendous
things.

00:04:27.639 --> 00:04:33.340
And for me it was this atmosphere of higher
purpose and moral ambiguity, that give Chrollo

00:04:33.340 --> 00:04:40.150
his undeniably intriguing and mysterious presence.
So it's fair to say I believe, that the religious

00:04:40.150 --> 00:04:46.590
hints here aren't exactly subtle. The point
however I think, is. Because in some ways

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:53.169
Togashi portrays Chrollo as Christ and in
others as the anti christ. He can value the

00:04:53.169 --> 00:04:59.159
lives of his comrades, but at the same time
slaughter wholesale without the blink of an

00:04:59.159 --> 00:05:04.060
eye. So let's talk about the deep message
behind Chrollo's character.

