00:06:06.530 --> 00:06:12.379
Now, we don't really know much about Chrollo's
childhood and why he relies so incredibly

00:06:12.379 --> 00:06:17.240
on fate. All we know about him is that he’s
from Meteor City, which has a lot of mystery

00:06:17.240 --> 00:06:25.990
built up around it, and which we know is a
place where people throw other people away.

00:06:25.990 --> 00:06:32.700
A place so dark and terrible, some don’t
even believe it exists.

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:37.630
Now even for me, it’s not too hard from
a psychological lens to see why someone who

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:43.919
grew up in such an environment would tell
themselves that fate governs everything and

00:06:43.919 --> 00:06:48.060
look for a higher purpose in life. Growing
up in a world of suffering and pain, this

00:06:48.060 --> 00:06:54.039
can be a source of hope and stability. All
you are going through has a reason and all

00:06:54.039 --> 00:06:59.020
the morally questionable things you have to
do in order to survive are not your fault,

00:06:59.020 --> 00:07:01.500
but part of a greater plan.

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:07.400
And in this darkest of places, Chrollo forms
the spiders, a sort of family, that shares

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:13.210
his beliefs and is a community of people who
care for, protect and respect each other.

00:07:13.210 --> 00:07:27.150
A chance to cast aside all their pain and
hardship. The group and its cause become everyone's

00:07:27.150 --> 00:07:32.360
purpose. I'm sure, no matter if you go to
a service or not, this is a concept you'll

00:07:32.360 --> 00:07:38.069
recognize from religion. In fact it's arguably
the most important part for many believers,

00:07:38.069 --> 00:07:43.270
having a community of people who share your
believes and help you through times of darkness

00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:44.270
and hardship.

00:07:44.270 --> 00:07:49.979
It is also no surprise then, that CHrollo
is so obsessed with Neon's ability to predict

00:07:49.979 --> 00:07:55.050
one's fate. Seeking her out was the only time
he ever diverted his attention from their

00:07:55.050 --> 00:08:07.370
mission in York New city. Chrollo's belief
that everything is pre-determined by fate,

00:08:07.370 --> 00:08:14.729
leads to his Jesus like ability to forgive
and accept. He doesn't see Judas in other

00:08:14.729 --> 00:08:19.620
words Hisoka as a traitor, when he starts
hunting down members of the Troupe and even

00:08:19.620 --> 00:08:25.199
himself, because Hisoka has no control over
his life.

00:08:25.199 --> 00:08:32.279
It's all been written beforehand. Hisoka is
just playing his role. So why would Chrollo

00:08:32.279 --> 00:08:38.760
hate him, if it's not his fault? And of course
forgiveness and acceptance are universally

00:08:38.760 --> 00:08:44.810
important concepts that are taught by many
religions. So up to this point, in my mind,

00:08:44.810 --> 00:08:50.890
Chrollo embodies some of the best things about
faith: Finding an altruistic purpose in life,

00:08:50.890 --> 00:08:56.480
gifting that purpose to others like him, forming
a caring community looking for a better life

00:08:56.480 --> 00:09:05.500
and being forgiving to others. The Jesus side
of chrollo.

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:22.330
But given all that, there is no denying that
THIS, is the person we're talking about here.

00:09:22.330 --> 00:09:28.040
[...] Chrollo IS one of the major antagonists
in the story, even though interestingly enough

00:09:28.040 --> 00:09:34.090
he only touches with our main characters very
scarcely. In fact Hisoka and Kurapika are

00:09:34.090 --> 00:09:40.040
the only characters who's arcs are deeply
involved with Chrollo, which is of course

00:09:40.040 --> 00:09:44.650
intriguing, because Hisoka is a major antagonistic
force himself.

00:09:44.650 --> 00:09:57.790
And be honest, I know you love two great villains
fighting each other, just as much as I do.

00:09:57.790 --> 00:10:02.510
Even though they both fall on the murderous
lunatic end of the chart, they vary quit a

00:10:02.510 --> 00:10:09.690
bit in their motivations and values. Chrollo
and Hisoka are Jesus and Judas. Unshakable

00:10:09.690 --> 00:10:15.760
order versus deliberate chaos. No value to
a single human life, so I might as well kill

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:21.310
them, vs. human life is the only thing that
gives my actions value,... so I might as well

00:10:21.310 --> 00:10:33.640
kill them. After all Hisoka is the embodiment
of lust, one of the seven deadly sins.

00:10:33.640 --> 00:10:41.060
And if Hisoka is lust, Chrollo is greed. He
likes to give off the appearance of the selfless

00:10:41.060 --> 00:10:48.030
leader that doesn't need anything. And yet
he is greedy beyond limits. He wants the money,

00:10:48.030 --> 00:10:54.520
he wants vast knowledge, he wants all the
worldly things. Chrollo was a man with nothing

00:10:54.520 --> 00:10:57.290
who now wants, everything.

00:10:57.290 --> 00:11:02.120
Someone SO obsessed with human nature, To
the point where he will use this obsession

00:11:02.120 --> 00:11:07.240
to manipulate another person, to get what
he wanted from them. He instilled himself

00:11:07.240 --> 00:11:12.260
to read books and observe the people around
him. Even using these books to pick certain

00:11:12.260 --> 00:11:15.760
personality traits for himself.

00:11:15.760 --> 00:11:27.820
Most telling however is of course his nen.
As we all know, nen usually reflects the users

00:11:27.820 --> 00:11:33.610
personality really well, and I was shocked
to find out that Chrollo has the greediest

00:11:33.610 --> 00:11:37.600
nen ability of them all, stealing others people's
powers.

00:11:37.600 --> 00:11:43.930
What turns Chrollo's good intentions and belief
against themselves, is his complete and unquestioning

00:11:43.930 --> 00:11:50.380
faith in them. Chrollo is convinced that everything
is predetermined. Everyone has their fixed

00:11:50.380 --> 00:11:56.440
role to play and thus it doesn't really matter
what he does, since it is fate guiding his

00:11:56.440 --> 00:12:04.190
hand anyways.

00:12:04.190 --> 00:12:08.330
Fully subscribing to his believes, as you
should be to my videos, means that to Chrollo

00:12:08.330 --> 00:12:14.800
humans are nothing but puppets. And he uses
this belief as a justification for all the

00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:22.030
atrocities he commits. And since he has incredible
power, he sees himself in a privileged position

00:12:22.030 --> 00:12:28.850
above other humans, chosen by fate to fulfill
the most special of roles. He thinks he's

00:12:28.850 --> 00:12:30.560
Jesus.

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:35.510
Interestingly enough, what Chrollo really
wants, just like Hisoka or Meruem, is fill

00:12:35.510 --> 00:12:41.510
the hole in their heart. The deep dark emptiness
within them, that threatens to drown them.

00:12:41.510 --> 00:12:46.420
Hisoka fills this with kicks, looking for
things that make him feel excited and alive

00:12:46.420 --> 00:12:52.620
by risking his own life aaaannd by making
others feel like shit as well, again more

00:12:52.620 --> 00:12:54.980
on that in his video.

00:12:54.980 --> 00:13:02.410
Meruem, actually meets Komugi, overcomes his
pride and manages to fill this hole ...before

00:13:02.410 --> 00:13:07.830
dying. And chrollo clings to his destined
role in the world and the belief that everything

00:13:07.830 --> 00:13:13.770
he does has a higher purpose. That there is
reason for all the pain and suffering in the

00:13:13.770 --> 00:13:20.440
world. And carrying out his role, he will
be the savior of all.

00:13:20.440 --> 00:13:25.280
The phantom troupe means so much to Chrollo,
because these people actually are all that

00:13:25.280 --> 00:13:30.800
really matters to him on a human level. They
are his true family and purpose. [...] But

00:13:30.800 --> 00:13:35.640
even though he acknowledges it himself, he
still tries to push himself away from others

00:13:35.640 --> 00:13:40.660
and cast aside his human side. Instead of
embracing his humanity and be vulnerable,

00:13:40.660 --> 00:13:44.390
he tries to make himself something more.

00:13:44.390 --> 00:13:50.000
This approach to life represents the darkest
side of religion and other doctrines in general.

00:13:50.000 --> 00:13:55.350
When you follow a belief so radically and
without question, that you lose side of the

00:13:55.350 --> 00:14:01.260
original good intent. It's a striking critique
by Togashi of all the violence that has been

00:14:01.260 --> 00:14:06.660
committed in the name of gods and states and
political systems throughout history. Seeing

00:14:06.660 --> 00:14:12.060
oneself above others and believing oneself
to be the only one that truly understands

00:14:12.060 --> 00:14:17.580
how the world works. Or, borrowing from another
popular franchise, doing it for the greater

00:14:17.580 --> 00:14:26.720
good.

00:14:26.720 --> 00:14:32.140
I'm sure you know in your gut, why Chrollo
and extremists belief in any doctrine are

00:14:32.140 --> 00:14:38.500
problematic. But, let me tell you anyway:
It's objectively immoral. It's immoral to

00:14:38.500 --> 00:14:43.740
murder in the name of a higher purpose or
the belief that all is predetermined.

00:14:43.740 --> 00:14:48.920
Hunter x Hunter is famous for exploring morality
through characters, that feel real, because

00:14:48.920 --> 00:14:53.680
they are morally grey. However, I think it
would be a grave misconception to think that

00:14:53.680 --> 00:14:59.620
Hunter x hunter beliefs that there is no such
thing as morality. In fact the opposite is

00:14:59.620 --> 00:15:05.010
true. What Togashi shows through the actions
of all his characters is that there is many

00:15:05.010 --> 00:15:12.440
ways to act good or badly, even within a character.

00:15:12.440 --> 00:15:18.480
But in the end, what determines a moral action,
is how it affects human well-being. You might

00:15:18.480 --> 00:15:24.130
have heard the famous phrase: Cogito ergo
sum. I think therefore I am. What this sentence

00:15:24.130 --> 00:15:30.100
really means, is that we all have no idea
to tell what is real. The world might be a

00:15:30.100 --> 00:15:37.870
simulation, we could be a brain in a jar or
like chrollo thinks, all is guided by fate.

00:15:37.870 --> 00:15:39.820
We just don't know.

00:15:39.820 --> 00:15:45.900
The only thing you can be sure of in this
moment right now, is that it feels like something

00:15:45.900 --> 00:15:51.420
to be you. The fact that you are experiencing
something right now is the only thing you

00:15:51.420 --> 00:15:59.220
know really exists. So whether you suffer
right now or not is the only thing that matters.

00:15:59.220 --> 00:16:05.950
Human well-being is what matters. The well-being
of all conscious creatures is what matters,

00:16:05.950 --> 00:16:11.730
even if we had no control over our lives.

00:16:11.730 --> 00:16:18.070
So, treating humans as puppets and killing
them for a higher purpose, goes against THE

00:16:18.070 --> 00:16:23.650
highest purpose there is. An objective morality.
And the fact that we had to go this deep to

00:16:23.650 --> 00:16:29.240
solve why he is evil, is why Chrollo is one
of my favorite villains ever.

00:16:29.240 --> 00:16:34.220
However, to really understand how Togashi
sees evil, you'll need to watch my video on

00:16:34.220 --> 00:16:35.750
Hisoka here as well.

